Theorem RL-DROP: scope-exit user @drop for a drop-glue value, gated on drop-glue existence INDEPENDENT of isScalar

  Preconditions:
    - RL-DROP governs the scope-exit user-`@drop` op for a value whose TYPE
      carries a user `@drop` (drop-glue), per Annex E §AIMS RC Emission:
      "A value whose type carries a user `@drop` SHALL receive EXACTLY ONE
      scope-exit user-drop CALL at its death point, gated on drop-glue
      existence INDEPENDENT of its RC repr. The user-drop op carries
      ref-count delta 0 (it is a `@drop` call, not an RC ref-count op)."
    - The RC dec rules (RL-2 / RL-4 / RL-5) all gate dec emission on
      `!isScalar`: a value whose monomorphized repr is `Scalar` carries no
      RC header and provably receives NO `RcDec` (that gating is the
      soundness basis VF-1's `RcOnScalar` invariant enforces). But a value's
      TYPE may carry drop-glue INDEPENDENT of its RC repr — a `Scalar`-repr
      struct (`type Guard = { id: int }` with `impl Guard: Drop`) has
      drop-glue yet no RC field.
    - The RC ops cannot express a scalar value's drop (an `RcDec` on a
      `Scalar` is rejected by VF-1), so the realization op set carries a
      SEPARATE `userDrop` op: a drop-glue CALL with ref-count delta 0.
      Because `userDrop` is RC-balance-neutral, the `!isScalar` RcDec
      invariant (RL-2/4/5) is preserved untouched — a scalar value still
      receives no `RcDec`, only the balance-neutral `@drop` call.
    - Shipped sites: the scope-exit op is realized as
      `RcStrategy::UserDrop` (ir/repr.rs), lowered from a whole-var
      `BurdenDec` for a scalar+drop-glue var by
      realize/emit_unified.rs::lower_burden_ops_to_rc; a never-used
      scalar+drop-glue local is admitted by
      lower/burden_lower/scan_orchestration.rs::emit_unused_scalar_user_drop_decs
      (RL-2 unused-owned dec). VF-1's check_rc_instr_scalar EXEMPTS
      `RcDec { strategy: UserDrop }` from `RcOnScalar`. The LLVM emitter
      (arc_emitter/rc_ops.rs::emit_rc_dec_user_drop) emits ONLY the user
      `@drop` call (invoke + re-raise-only cleanup pad), no field walk, no
      `ori_rc_dec`.

  Soundness property:
    Forall value v at its death point with drop inputs
    (hasUserDrop, isScalar):

      (P1) Emission decision: RL-DROP emits a scope-exit `userDrop` for v
           iff hasUserDrop, INDEPENDENT of isScalar. A drop-glue value
           always drops; a `@drop`-less value never does (whatever its repr).

      (P2) Scalar-soundness: a `Scalar`-repr value with drop-glue emits the
           balance-neutral `userDrop` AND NO `RcDec`. Its RC balance is 0 —
           the `@drop` runs without ever placing an `RcDec` on a scalar
           (which VF-1 would reject). The `!isScalar` RcDec invariant
           (RL-2/4/5) is preserved, NOT weakened: `userDrop` is a distinct
           op category (delta 0), so emitting it perturbs no RC-balance
           ledger.

      (P3) Exactly-once: a drop-glue value's death-point lifecycle carries
           exactly ONE `userDrop` op — never duplicated (no double-drop) and
           never elided (the cure: the prior RC-only realization
           elided a scalar value's drop because every RC dec is
           `!isScalar`-gated).

  Proof obligation:
    Discharged in the kernel-checked Lean corpus (AimsProof.Realization,
    §8.1 RL-DROP block) — the authority per arc.md §Realization-semantics
    grounding. The `.proof` is the human-readable companion; the compiled
    Lean is the verified artifact.

    Part (P1) — emission decision:
      RLDROP_emit_on_drop_glue (rldrop_emits_user_drop d = d.hasUserDrop),
      RLDROP_scalar_value_still_drops (forall isScalar, hasUserDrop implies emit),
      RLDROP_no_glue_no_drop (forall isScalar, NOT hasUserDrop implies no emit).

    Part (P2) — scalar-soundness (balance ledger):
      RLDROP_user_drop_balance_neutral (rcBalance [RcOp.userDrop] = 0),
      RLDROP_scalar_lifecycle_sound (a scalar drop-glue value's lifecycle =
      [userDrop] only, balance 0, NO RcDec — the `!isScalar` invariant held).

    Part (P3) — exactly-once:
      RLDROP_exactly_once_on_glue (rldrop_lifecycle length 1 on drop-glue
      regardless of isScalar; length 0 without drop-glue).

    Negative-direction witness (the cured bug, REJECTED):
      A scalar drop-glue value's RC-only realization (no `userDrop` op,
      `RcDec` `!isScalar`-gated to nothing) emits ZERO drop ops — the
      `@drop` is silently elided. Rejected by RLDROP_exactly_once_on_glue
      (the scalar drop-glue lifecycle has length 1, not 0).

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: companion to the kernel-checked AimsProof.Realization §8.1 RL-DROP block (RLDROP_emit_on_drop_glue / RLDROP_scalar_value_still_drops / RLDROP_no_glue_no_drop / RLDROP_user_drop_balance_neutral / RLDROP_scalar_lifecycle_sound / RLDROP_exactly_once_on_glue), which is the verified discharge; a dedicated section_08 engine for the userDrop op category is future work
